ge, exclusions and any bad-faith questions stay separate legal issues."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do I still deal with my adjuster during appraisal?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Often yes, for payments and paperwork. The amount in dispute, though, is worked out between the two appraisers and, if needed, the umpire."}}],"@id":"https://mississippiinsuranceappraiser.com/our-appraisal-services/appraisal-demand-representation/#faq","isPartOf":{"@id":"https://mississippiinsuranceappraiser.com/our-appraisal-services/appraisal-demand-representation/#webpage"}},{"@type":"Service","name":"Appraisal Demand Representation","serviceType":"Appraisal Demand Representation","description":"Appraisal clause representation in Mississippi: we serve as your appointed appraiser from the written demand to a two-of-three award.","provider":{"@id":"https://mississippiinsuranceappraiser.com/#business"},"areaServed":{"@type":"State","name":"Mississippi"},"url":"https://mississippiinsuranceappraiser.com/our-appraisal-services/appraisal-demand-representation/","image":"https://mississippiinsuranceappraiser.com/assets/img/photos/consultation.webp","@id":"https://mississippiinsuranceappraiser.com/our-appraisal-services/appraisal-demand-representation/#service"}]}</script>
